print_zapfast_post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF2'
zapfast setup:

  Launch it and, on the phone, open WhatsApp > Linked devices > Link a
  device, then point the camera at the code (or link with your phone
  number instead). The chats sync to a local archive on the first link.

  Keep your desktop keyring unlocked so ZapFast Plus can open its
  encrypted archive. On Linux this needs a Secret Service provider
  (GNOME Keyring or KeePassXC with Secret Service enabled).

  This is ZapFast Plus, a personal fork. It installs the same `zapfast`
  binary, launcher entry and state folder as the upstream package, so the
  two cannot be installed together.

Repo: https://github.com/lucasapolinarioo/zapfast-plus
Chat: https://discord.gg/8MnXbuKWaq
EOF2
}

post_install() {
  print_zapfast_post_install
}

post_upgrade() {
  print_zapfast_post_install
}
